From 46e479632235bb2fc601c772c34cd4a590172003 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brunduk <nikolai.viktorovich@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 14:52:34 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] 360 viewer: trigger pause, grip recenter, hold-to-quit,
 themes - on the profile the G2 actually uses

The G2 lands on oculus/touch_controller, not microsoft/motion_controller:
Monado's profile selection walks the driver's binding_profiles[] remaps in
order and takes the first profile the app suggested bindings for, and the
G2 driver's first remap is Touch. Every player binding suggested only
under the WMR profile was therefore dead. All player actions now live in
the Touch block too: thumbstick seek, trigger pause/resume, squeeze-value
recenter (boolean-on-float, runtime thresholds at 0.7), and menu
(left-hand-only on Touch) as quit.

Quit is now hold-to-confirm (~1.5s, red fill bar top of view) instead of
an instant exit on a button that is easy to hit by accident. Recenter
(also keyboard enter) makes the current gaze direction the new forward,
yaw only. HELLO_XR_THEME=daylight|night picks the color of the empty
space outside the content, which the skybox shader now discards instead
of painting black - black-out-of-frame read as "tracking broke". On
profile attach the log prints the active profile per hand and each
action's bound sources, so a dead input is diagnosable from the terminal.

Verified on hardware: left-controller stick/trigger/menu-hold all work.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
